  "acceptance_criteria": [
    "Railway contains exactly one intended web service, one API service, and one PostgreSQL service for the finals environment, with database traffic on private networking.",
    "The web service serves SPA routes on refresh and uses an environment-defined API origin without exposing server secrets.",
    "The API reports process liveness separately from readiness, and readiness fails when PostgreSQL or the required Alembic revision is unavailable.",
    "A backend write persists through API restart and remains visible after browser refresh.",
    "Reset/reseed restores the controlled workflow seed while preserving valid Epic authorization and last-known-good snapshot records by default.",
    "Missing required variables or a failed migration prevents readiness and produces actionable redacted logs.",
    "Frontend and backend watch paths avoid rebuilding the unrelated service.",
    "A deployment is reported live only after Railway status is SUCCESS and the web, API, database, migration, CORS, and persistence checks pass."
  ],
